# ==============================================================================================
# slatwall-ts — environment template for the extracted Catalog service.
#
# This is a COMMITTED TEMPLATE. It declares the NAME of every environment variable the service
# reads and deliberately carries NO VALUES. Copy it, then fill the copy in, for work against a
# live database:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# The copy is ignored, this template is not: slatwall-ts/.gitignore:L37 lists the exact
# filename `.env` rather than a wildcard, so a filled-in file can never be committed while the
# names stay under version control. No credential is hardcoded anywhere in this port, and none
# is committed here — configuration is environment-driven end to end (AAP 0.8.3.9).
#
# Nothing below is needed to BUILD, TYPE-CHECK, LINT or TEST this subtree. `npm run typecheck`,
# `npm run build`, `npm run lint` and `npm test` all succeed with no `.env` present and no
# database reachable, because src/config/env.ts validates the connection facts without ever
# opening a connection, the Google integration is a stub that makes no network call, and the
# unit tests run against hand-written in-memory doubles. A value is required only at the point
# where a real MySQL connection is actually opened.
#
# WHERE THESE VARIABLES ARE READ
# ------------------------------
# In exactly one place. src/config/env.ts is the sole reader of the process environment in this
# subtree, and configuration then flows one way only (AAP 0.4.3.5):
#
#     environment -> src/config/env.ts -> src/config/database.ts -> src/config/container.ts
#                    reads + validates    module-scope mysql2 pool   wires the object graph
#
# Every layer below the config layer — domain, ports, adapters, services, validation and
# integrations — receives what it needs by constructor injection and never reaches for the
# environment itself. The list below is therefore exhaustive by construction: it is exactly the
# key set read at src/config/env.ts:L419-L423, no more and no less. A name declared here that
# nothing reads, and a name read there that is missing here, are both defects.
#
# ==============================================================================================
# PROVENANCE — the legacy application recorded only FOUR connection-related values in source
# ==============================================================================================
# The legacy CFML application never held connection details in source at all. It named a
# ColdFusion/Railo datasource and let the application server resolve it out of band. Across the
# whole legacy tree the datasource struct has exactly three members — `.name`, `.username` and
# `.password` — and the bootstrap republishes those plus the ORM dialect:
#
#   config/configApplication.cfm:L2  `<cfset this.datasource.name = "Slatwall" />`
#   Application.cfc:L78              publishes `datasource`         <- this.datasource.name
#   Application.cfc:L81              publishes `datasourceUsername` <- this.datasource.username
#   Application.cfc:L84              publishes `datasourcePassword` <- this.datasource.password
#   Application.cfc:L87              publishes `databaseType`       <- this.ormSettings.dialect
#   org/Hibachi/Hibachi.cfc:L12-L13  set username and password to the EMPTY STRING
#
# Those four values are the entire derivation basis for the names below. Because
# org/Hibachi/Hibachi.cfc:L12-L13 sets both credentials to `""`, there is no legacy credential
# to carry across and nothing to inherit — which is why every value below is blank rather than
# seeded.
#
# ==============================================================================================
# DECISION — the three-way runtime dialect probe is collapsed to a fixed MySQL target
# ==============================================================================================
# config/configORM.cfm:L3-L14 chose the persistence dialect at RUNTIME. L3 probed the server
# with `<cfdbinfo ... type="Version" name="dbVersion">`, then three branches inspected the
# reported product name: L9-L10 selected "MySQL", L11-L12 "MicrosoftSQLServer" and L13-L14
# "Oracle10g" — with no else-branch, so an unrecognised product left the dialect unset.
#
# This port targets MySQL only. The Sw* schema is retained unchanged and read and written
# through `mysql2`, the single runtime dependency, so the branch is resolved at DESIGN time
# rather than at configuration time (AAP 0.4.1.3 — "a fixed MySQL target with the branch
# documented").
#
# The consequence is stated explicitly so it cannot be mistaken for an oversight: there is
# deliberately NO DB_DIALECT and NO DATABASE_TYPE variable here, and none is read anywhere in
# src/**. Offering one would advertise a portability this port does not implement. No database
# engine version is asserted either; the legacy repository pins none.
#
# ==============================================================================================
# DOCUMENTED ABSENCES — host, port and schema name are NOT DECLARED in legacy source
# ==============================================================================================
# "Slatwall" at config/configApplication.cfm:L2 is a ColdFusion/Railo DATASOURCE NAME: an alias
# registered in the application server's administrator, which the server resolves out of band
# to a JDBC URL, a schema, a user and a password. It is NOT a schema name, NOT a host, NOT a
# port and NOT a user, so it is never used as one. It appears in this file only in comments,
# only with its locator. admin/views/main/nodatasource.cfm:L12 confirms the indirection: it
# instructs an operator to define the datasource NAME and nothing else.
#
# The evidence is the absence of everything else. A search of the legacy tree for a JDBC URL, a
# port number or a `.host`/`.port`/`.database` member of the datasource struct returns no
# match anywhere, and the four datasource reference sites listed under PROVENANCE declare no
# host, port, schema, username or password value between them.
#
# So DB_HOST, DB_PORT and DB_NAME are new here by necessity, not by choice, and they are left
# BLANK rather than guessed. Nothing below is defaulted — not the schema name, not the host and
# not the port; the conventional MySQL port number in particular is nowhere in this file.
# Supplying a plausible-looking value would assert a fact the source does not state, and the
# standard is to record the absence instead (AAP 0.9.3, IR-12).
#
# ==============================================================================================
# DELIBERATE OMISSIONS — no tuning knobs are exposed, because the source pins none
# ==============================================================================================
# There is no pool-sizing variable and no connection-lifetime variable of any kind. AAP 0.4.1.3
# is explicit and binding on src/config/database.ts: "pool sizing is not carried over because
# the legacy application delegates pooling to the CF/Railo server and pins nothing in source."
# The pool is created once at module scope so it is reused across warm invocations, and it is
# handed exactly the five values below and nothing else.
#
# Any figure written here would be invented, so none is: this file states no latency,
# throughput, capacity or service-level number anywhere (IR-12). The two timing values the
# legacy source does declare are request-scoped controls that belong with the execution-model
# mismatches in the README, not with connection configuration.
#
# ==============================================================================================
# VARIABLES — names only; every value is intentionally blank
# ==============================================================================================
# Listed in the order src/config/env.ts validates them, which is the order in which a missing
# or malformed value is reported.

# Connection target. Not declared anywhere in legacy source — see DOCUMENTED ABSENCES above.
# Both must be non-blank before a connection is opened; DB_PORT must be a TCP port number.
DB_HOST=
DB_PORT=

# Schema holding the existing Sw* tables. This service reads and writes that schema and neither
# creates nor migrates it. Must be non-blank before a connection is opened. NOT the datasource
# name from config/configApplication.cfm:L2 — see DOCUMENTED ABSENCES above.
DB_NAME=

# Credentials, mapped from Application.cfc:L81 and Application.cfc:L84
# (`this.datasource.username` / `this.datasource.password`). org/Hibachi/Hibachi.cfc:L12-L13
# sets both to the empty string in legacy source, so NO value is committed here.
#
# These two are the only variables that may legitimately stay empty at run time: the validator
# requires them to be PRESENT but permits an empty string, which reproduces the legacy `""`
# exactly. Empty and absent are therefore different states, and only absent is an error.
DB_USER=
DB_PASSWORD=
